## Context
Memory is written straight into the live `~/.claude` checkout (the only path the
write guard allows) and left uncommitted. Upstream also edits the same files
(MEMORY.md indexes, `/dream`, archived tickets), so `sync-local-main.sh` refuses to
fast-forward and merged harness changes never reach running sessions.

Observed twice in two days:
- doudou, 2026-09-23: 165 commits behind; harness PR #968 merged but not live.
- padme, 2026-09-24: 150 commits behind; `scripts/scoped-check.py` was missing, so
  a search-works lane could run `make check-diff` only from a borrowed harness
  worktree. The one blocking file was a locally appended log line on ticket 0207,
  which upstream had closed and moved.

Per-host manual reconciles (backup, restore, ff, re-apply) fix the symptom only.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Memory written during a session reaches origin without leaving the live
      checkout dirty, or the sync tolerates it (e.g. ff when dirty paths don't
      collide, and a named report when they do)
- [ ] A live checkout that falls behind origin/main is reported at session start
      on every host, with the blocking paths named
- [ ] `make check` passes
